{
  "requirement": "`InspectionContext::read` returns the node's complete application-defined\n`D::NodeContent`, or the domain's read error.\n\nThe SDK's `read_node` tool accepts a known node's `NodePath` and returns its\ncontents formatted under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `read_node.behavior`. I did not find a gap.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `InspectionContext::read` returns the node's complete `D::NodeContent`.\n2. `InspectionContext::read` returns the domain's read error when the read fails.\n3. The `read_node` tool accepts a known node's `NodePath` and returns its contents formatted via `NodeContents::format`, as `judge.rendering` describes.\n4. Under `judge.rendering`, a preparation failure during a `read_node` call is returned to the agent as a tool error, so the agent can recover.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Complete contents (1):** `tests/validation.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` reads two cases through `InspectionContext::read`. The first is an empty string. The second is a long multi-byte Unicode string of roughly 16,400 characters, which is longer than the 8,192-character page size. It asserts `contents.format() == original` and that the snapshot content and fingerprint match. It also changes the domain's content afterwards and checks that the returned contents still equal the original, so the retained observation is the same one that was read.\n- **Domain read error (2):** the same test asserts `failed.read(&9).unwrap_err() == \"missing\"` and that no dependency is recorded. `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` also asserts that reading missing node 2 returns an error. It checks the successful reads and the read counts too.\n- **Tool returns formatted contents for a known path (3):**\n  - In `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`, the `ParallelConversations` provider calls `read_node` with `{\"path\":{\"segments\":[node]}}`. It asserts that the delivered history contains that conversation's `…-CONTENTS` text, which comes from the domain formatter. It also asserts that the other conversation's text is absent. The recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprints match the formatted content.\n  - In `fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]`, a `read_node` call on an 18,000-character node is followed by `get_node_page`. The test asserts that the recorded fingerprint equals the full formatted content. That covers the text and fingerprint describing the same observation.\n- **Tool error and recovery (4):** `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes the formatter fail. It asserts that the next request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, name `read_node`, and the text \"unsupported node contents\". It also asserts that the agent continues and submits successfully, and that no dependency is recorded.\n\n**Unmarked tests**\n`fn[graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change]` is marked for `read_node.inputs` but not for this requirement. That is not a gap, because the marked tests already cover the obligations above.\n\nNo `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
